<title>INDIA: Indian ports handle 19.06 mln tonnes cargo in July.</title>
<headline>Indian ports handle 19.06 mln tonnes cargo in July.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major Indian ports handled 19.06 million tonnes of cargo in July against a target of 18.43 million tonnes and compared with 17.90 million in the same month in 1996, the Surface Transport ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A ministry statement said the ports handled 80.84 million tonnes of cargo between April and July against a target of 77.51 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The ports handled 72.53 million tonnes of cargo during April-July 1996, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The country has 11 major ports.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
